<section class="split">
  <div>
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>BrightHope Foundation was founded in 2015 by a small group of volunteers who believed that no child should miss school, no family should go hungry, and no one should skip treatment because they cannot afford it.</p>
    <p>What began as weekend food drives in one neighbourhood has grown into a registered non-profit running 12 programs across three districts — and it remains powered by people like you.</p>
  </div>
  <img src="/images/community.jpg" alt="BrightHope volunteers working together">
</section>

<section class="section" style="padding-left:0; padding-right:0;">
  <h2>Our values</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-3" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
    <article class="card"><div class="card-body">
      <span class="card-tag">Value</span>
      <h3>Dignity first</h3>
      <p>We serve people with respect, never as charity cases. Everything we do preserves the dignity of the families we support.</p>
    </div></article>
    <article class="card"><div class="card-body">
      <span class="card-tag">Value</span>
      <h3>Total transparency</h3>
      <p>Every rupee is tracked and reported. We publish impact updates and welcome questions about how funds are used.</p>
    </div></article>
    <article class="card"><div class="card-body">
      <span class="card-tag">Value</span>
      <h3>Local first</h3>
      <p>Programs are designed with and for local communities, so solutions fit real needs and outlast the funding cycle.</p>
    </div></article>
  </div>
</section>

